# KNOWN GAP (todo/t0727): under `--sanitize --backend=llvm`, GENERATED USER CODE
# CARRIES NO SANITIZER INSTRUMENTATION. Only the C runtime blob does.
#
# `--sanitize` on that backend reaches two of the three compile/link steps: the
# runtime `cc -c`, and the final link. It cannot reach the step in between,
# which is `llc` — and `llc` consumes finished IR, so ASan's instrumentation
# pass has already not run by the time it is invoked. Emitting instrumented IR
# means the LLVM backend attaching `sanitize_address` itself and the result
# surviving the instrumentation passes; neither happens today.
#
# ── WHAT THAT COSTS, from the measured coverage split ──
#   CAUGHT on this lane: every memory leak (LeakSanitizer intercepts the
#     allocator, so instrumentation is irrelevant to it); UAF, double-free and
#     overflow whose free OR faulting access goes through the runtime — which
#     is most of Gorget's heap traffic; interceptor classes (memcpy, strlen, …);
#     UB inside the C runtime.
#   MISSED on this lane: a stack-buffer-overflow in generated user code; a
#     direct load or store from a user frame into freed heap that touches no
#     runtime function; UBSan on generated user code.
#
# ── WHY THIS FIXTURE PINS IT STRUCTURALLY RATHER THAN BEHAVIOURALLY ──
#
# A behavioural repro would need a program that actually commits one of the
# missed defects, which in safe Gorget means leaning on some OTHER compiler bug
# to produce the UAF — and that repro would then go green the day THAT bug is
# fixed, silently ceasing to pin this gap while still reading as coverage. The
# structural pin has no such dependency: it asserts the mechanism itself, holds
# for any program at all, and can only change when this gap is actually closed.
#
# The program below therefore only has to contain ordinary user-code loads and
# stores — a struct field write and read, an arithmetic local, a call. On the C
# backend all of it is instrumented, necessarily and without measurement, since
# user code and runtime are ONE translation unit handed to `cc -fsanitize=…`.
# On the LLVM backend they are two objects and only one is instrumented.
#
# INTENDED (what the `#[ignore]`d test asserts, and what fails today):
#   GORGET_KEEP_RUNTIME=1 gg build --sanitize --backend=llvm <this>
#   => __gorget_user_<stem>.o references __asan_report_*
# MEASURED TODAY: the runtime object carries 10 such references, the user
# object carries 0.
#
# Correct stdout on every backend, sanitized or not: `9`.
# GRADUATES to a live regression fixture the round t0727 is fixed.

struct Point:
    int x
    int y

int shift_sum(Point p, int d):
    int a = p.x + d
    int b = p.y + d
    return a + b

void main():
    Point p = Point(1, 2)
    print(shift_sum(p, 3))
